\title{Finite incidence supports and a small dense candidate family}
\taxon{Development}
\meta{layer}{human}
\meta{source}{Kernel/Augmented/GeneratingFiniteExactness.lean}
\tag{foundation}
\tag{augmented}

\p{This continues \ref{augmented-arity-nerve} under \ref{dec-kr-0015}, \ref{dec-kr-0018} and \ref{at-fd-0007}. It supplies an algebraic candidate family of finite generating incidence diagrams. It does not designate a canonical minimal pasting format.}
\p{\code{Face} enumerates the generator itself and every incident vertex, vertical side and horizontal edge. \code{faceArrow_surjective} proves every incidence arrow occurs in this finite list, even for nullary inputs and empty outputs. Finiteness is over all source sorts together. Both endpoint rows and both vertical sides remain present for \code{(0,0)} cells.}
\p{\code{finiteSupport} closes a finite collection of generators under all incidence maps. \code{finite_subfunctor_elements} proves the resulting total collection of objects, vertical/horizontal edges and cells across all arities is finite. \code{presheafIsFinite_iff_finite_elements} identifies Mathlib's finite-generation condition with finite total incidence in this base; \code{finite_range_elements} proves maps from finite incidence data have finite images.}
\p{\code{finiteSupportDiagram} orders the finite generating sets by inclusion. Its index is filtered, and \code{finiteSupportIsColimit} proves the canonical inclusion cocone is a colimit: single-generator supports cover every element, and unions identify overlaps at a common finite stage. \code{finitelyPresentable_iff_finite_elements} then characterizes the finitely presentable presheaves exactly as the finite incidence presheaves. The forward implication factors the identity through one finite support; the reverse uses the finite category-of-elements presentation by representables.}
\p{\code{FiniteIncidence} is a small model of this full category, and \code{finiteIncidenceGraphs} is its fully faithful dense inclusion into explicit generating graphs. The universe change used to invoke presheaf local presentability is an actual category equivalence. \code{finiteIncidenceNerve_full} and \code{finiteIncidenceNerve_essImage_iff} apply the existing augmented nerve theorem to this candidate. Density is now a conclusion for this family; pointwise invertibility of its canonical monad comparison remains an explicit hypothesis.}
\p{\strong{Remaining:} prove filtered-colimit preservation by the augmented generating monad. The specialized finite-arity argument now proves this is equivalent to canonical-comparison invertibility. The checked colimit decomposition is in the base; it does not prove the monad preserves it. Finite raw cell-term leaves alone omit the complete incidence and equation-witness obligations. No normalization, generic/free factorization, Reedy/elegance or labelled diagram-model theorem is asserted. This partial evidence preserves the current statements, versions and proposed statuses of AT-FD-7, \ref{at-kr-0002} and \ref{at-kr-0008}. Cites: \ref{dec-rt-0030}, \ref{dec-wf-0008}, \ref{dec-wf-0010}.}

\p{\strong{Finitary exactness reduction:} \code{GeneratingFiniteNerve} proves filtered-colimit preservation by the finite-incidence base nerve, factorization through finite supports, and finite-stage witnesses for equality of maps. \code{freeNerveComparison_eq} identifies the actual comparison on each arity of a fully faithful family with the representable Kan-extension isomorphism. \code{isIso_of_finiteIncidence} detects isomorphisms of filtered-colimit-preserving functors on the small finite family. Consequently, \code{finiteIncidence_exactness_iff_finitary} proves global canonical-comparison invertibility equivalent to filtered-colimit preservation by the actual generating monad. The augmented nerve theorem follows under this one remaining hypothesis; finitarity itself and the labelled diagram model remain open. Acceptance statements, versions and statuses are unchanged.}
